You can have 
```rust
struct WindowCommands { /*todo*/ }

pub trait CommandsExt {
    fn window(&mut self) -> WindowCommands;
}

impl CommandsExt for Commands {
    fn window(&mut self) -> WindowCommands { todo!() }
}
```
in `bevy_window` without changing `bevy_ecs`. If the trait then is in bevy_window's prelude, everyone that has the window feature active and imports `bevy::prelude::*` has access to `Commands::window`.
